# "Whenever you sacrifice a land" is exactly that (CR 701.21a): a land of yours destroyed by an opponent's Wasteland is
# not sacrificed, a Lotus Petal sacrificed for mana is not a land, and neither makes a Beast. Only the Forest Bot1 then
# sacrifices to Baloth Prime's own ability does: one tapped Beast, and the untap is spent on a stun counter. Bot2's own
# Wasteland sacrificing itself as its cost is an opponent's land and triggers nothing either.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Baloth Prime
Lotus Petal
Bazaar of Baghdad
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Wasteland
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Lotus Petal.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Baloth Prime.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Wasteland.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Bazaar of Baghdad.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Wasteland.Activate(Bazaar of Baghdad; Ability: Destroy)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Graveyard = Bazaar of Baghdad
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 6
Bot1.Battlefield.Lotus Petal.Activate(Color: Green)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
? Bot1.Battlefield.Baloth Prime.Counters.Stun = 5
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Baloth Prime.Activate
Bot1.Choose(Forest)

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Emerald; Mox Pearl; Mox Ruby; Baloth Prime; Beast Token
Bot1.Battlefield.Baloth Prime.Counters.Stun = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Beast Token.Tapped = true
Bot1.Life = 22
